--- final message ---
I fixed the two audit findings and the figure-manifest error. The paper compiles to 11 pages with no errors. The canonical figure validator couldn't run in this workspace (it imports `src.orchestrator`, which isn't available here), so the figure-manifest fix is unchecked. The reference check passed, and the evidence verifier reports zero dangling references (50 total).

- **Introduction wording:** I dropped "attained … only by bottlenecked graphs such as paths and lollipops". It now says the bound is tight up to a constant factor on some graphs such as paths and cycles, and overshoots by a growing factor on dense graphs. I added a matching claim to `claims_grounding.json`.
- **Clip limitation:** The sentence saying the clip at 10 "would hide very large failures" contradicted the paper's own bound, so I replaced it. The 0.181 family-macro value limits any single test graph's error to about 4.35 (a factor of about 78). The clip therefore cannot have been binding. The limitation that per-graph and per-family errors weren't retained is kept.
- **Figure manifest:** `closed_form_gap` had empty `source_ids`. I set it to `final.metric.bound_macro_log_mae`, the sealed bound comparator. The figure itself is analytic, so this is a loose link to the empirical comparator.

The soft warnings about figure font size (7.7 pt) and PNG width (1500 px) are not addressed. The manuscript references the PDFs, so I left them.

I appended the repair entry to `memory.md`, `global_memory/memory.md` and `global_memory/memory.jsonl`.
